WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
On rocky shores in Scotland, two kinds
of barnacle grow on the same stretch of

2
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.740
rock.

3
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.270
One is found only high up.

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.490
The other covers the
middle and the lower shore.

5
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.270
Yet the high-shore barnacle can
survive on the lower rocks too.

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.770
So why is only one of them
ever found down there?

7
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.200
In this mission, you'll find
out why a niche is a role,

8
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.810
not a place, using a koala.

9
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.880
Then you'll watch two tiny
species that eat the same food:

10
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.970
first grown apart, then grown together.

11
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.870
Your mission: explain why only one kind
of barnacle is ever found on the lower

12
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.560
shore.
